        <body>
            <div xml:id="d597">

                <pb facs="1025" n="929" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg929"/>

                <head>No. 595.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">General Sickles to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation in Spain</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-11-12"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 12, 1873</date>.
                        (Received December 8.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 815.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to forward a copy of a
                    note passed to the minister <pb facs="1026" n="930" xml:id="pg930"/> of state
                    yesterday, requesting that any American citizens in custody of the authorities
                    at Santiago de Cuba be allowed all the privileges guaranteed to them by the
                    seventh article of the treaty of 1795, and that the consul of the United States
                    at that place be permitted to have free communication with the accused. This
                    suggestion seemed to me proper, in view of what happened in March last in the
                    case of the sailors of the bark Union, and your instructions in that case.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer><signed>D. E. SICKLES.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d597-a1.xml" xpointer="d597-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
